  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The annual budget for ChefLand has been announced and people are concerned about the modification in capital gain tax.\n\nGiven that the capital gain tax changed from X%X \\%X% to Y%Y \\%Y%, find whether it has `INCREASED`, `DECREASED`, or remained the `SAME`.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input consists of two space-separated integers XXX and YYY denoting the previous and new value of capital gain tax.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput on a new line:\n\n\n\n`INCREASED`, if the capital gain tax has increased;\n`DECREASED`, if the capital gain tax has decreased;\n`SAME`, if the capital gain tax remained the same.\n\nYou may print each character in uppercase or lowercase. For example, the strings `SAME`, `same`, `Same`, and `sAmE` would be considered identical.",
    "constraints": [
      "10≤X,Y≤3010 \\leq X, Y \\leq 3010≤X,Y≤30"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10 12",
        "output": "INCREASED",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe updated value of capital gain tax is higher, thus it has increased."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "30 25",
        "output": "DECREASED",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe updated value of capital gain tax is lower, thus it has decreased."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "15 15",
        "output": "SAME",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe updated value of capital gain tax is same as the previous value."
      }
    ]
  },
